{
  "date": "2026-09-28",
  "scope": "Windows' exception filter after a stack overflow on the main thread: the fault is noted, the frame left, and the fault reported from the frame's abort point as the ERR_DROP every other access violation gets, with the stack's guard page put back; checked by a harness test, on the stable win32-dev client and dedicated server, and on a build without the node-tree check against the damaged trees that crashed every profile in the node-tree record.",
  "found": {
    "record": "docs/fntech3/2026-09-27-bsp-node-trees.md",
    "symptom": "eight crashes with 0xC0000005 at fntech3.exe _chkstk+0x27, below Com_sprintf in ExceptionFilter: the filter ran on the exhausted stack and its report faulted again"
  },
  "change": {
    "files": [
      "code/win32/win_main.cpp",
      "code/qcommon/common.c",
      "code/qcommon/qcommon.h"
    ],
    "tests": [
      "tests/windows_stack_overflow_tests.py"
    ],
    "scripts": [
      "scripts/probe_stack_overflow.py"
    ],
    "filter": "ExceptionFilter keeps a small frame; on EXCEPTION_STACK_OVERFLOW on the main thread it stores the address and calls Com_ErrorAfterUnwind(ReportStackOverflow); on another thread it restores the desktop and returns EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH; every other code goes to ReportException, which is the old filter's body",
    "unwind": "Com_ErrorAfterUnwind moves an active print redirect into a static buffer, unlinks native modules' exception registrations as Com_Error does, and longjmps to abortframe; Com_Init and Com_Frame call Com_RaiseUnwoundError first at their abort point",
    "report": "ReportStackOverflow calls _resetstkoflw, then ReportException(EXCEPTION_STACK_OVERFLOW, address): the ERR_DROP 'Unhandled exception caught / Exception Code: STACK_OVERFLOW / Exception Address: module@offset'",
    "reserve": "InstallExceptionFilter calls SetThreadStackGuarantee(32768) on the main thread before SetUnhandledExceptionFilter",
    "harness": "developer-only 'crash stack' (Com_OverflowStack) beside the existing 'crash'"
  },
